        <body>
            <div xml:id="d681">

                <pb facs="0718" n="668" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg668"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Broadhead to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1893-10-25"><hi rendition="#italic">October
                                25, 1893</hi></date>. (Received November 6.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 20.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Mr. Lachenal, chief of the department of
                    foreign affairs for the Swiss Confederation, having returned to Berne and
                    informed me officially that he has again assumed the discharge of the duties of
                    his office, I submitted to him the inclosed communication in regard to the case
                    of Constance Madeleine His, and shall expect an answer as speedily as the grave
                    aspect which the case has assumed will admit.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James Broadhead.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d681-a1.xml" xpointer="d681-a1"/>
